    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Subordination, connectors and punctuation",
     "texto": [
      "The conjunctions **że**, **ponieważ** and **chociaż** introduce subordinate clauses. In Polish they are separated from the main clause by a comma: **Poinformowano, że…**; **Zostaliśmy, ponieważ…**",
      "Relative clauses with **który/która/które** pick up a noun and are also set off by a comma. Choose the connector according to the logical relation; do not use a cause when the text expresses concession."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
